#### Issue #485: refactor: remove artificial delay in heartbeat test

## Summary

The heartbeat test contains an artificial delay using `setTimeout`, which violates our code quality guidelines in `specs/bad-smell.md` sections 5 and 10.

## Why Artificial Delays Are Harmful

- Cause test flakiness and slow CI/CD pipelines
- Mask actual race conditions that should be fixed
- Tests should handle real async behavior properly
- Delays indicate a design issue that should be addressed

## Instance to Fix

### `apps/web/app/api/webhooks/agent/heartbeat/__tests__/route.test.ts:354`

```typescript
// ❌ Current - artificial delay to ensure different timestamps
it("should handle multiple consecutive heartbeats", async () => {
  // ... setup code ...

  // First heartbeat
  await POST(request1, { params: Promise.resolve({ runId }) });

  // Wait 10ms to ensure different timestamps
  await new Promise((resolve) => setTimeout(resolve, 10));

  // Second heartbeat
  await POST(request2, { params: Promise.resolve({ runId }) });

  // ... assertions ...
});
```

## Recommended Solutions

### Option 1: Mock the timestamp source
```typescript
// ✅ Control time at the source
const mockNow = vi.spyOn(Date, "now");
mockNow.mockReturnValueOnce(1000);

await POST(request1, { params: Promise.resolve({ runId }) });

mockNow.mockReturnValueOnce(2000);

await POST(request2, { params: Promise.resolve({ runId }) });
```

### Option 2: Pass timestamp as parameter
If the API accepts a timestamp parameter, use that instead of relying on system time.

### Option 3: Query and compare behavior, not timestamps
```typescript
// ✅ Test the behavior, not the timing
const response1 = await POST(request1, { params: Promise.resolve({ runId }) });
const response2 = await POST(request2, { params: Promise.resolve({ runId }) });

// Assert that both succeeded and state was updated
expect(response1.status).toBe(200);
expect(response2.status).toBe(200);

// If timestamp ordering matters, verify via the response or DB state
const finalState = await getRunState(runId);
expect(finalState.heartbeatCount).toBe(2);
```

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Remove the `setTimeout` delay from the test
- [ ] Implement deterministic alternative (timestamp mocking or behavior-based testing)
- [ ] Test remains reliable without flakiness
- [ ] All tests pass after changes

## References

- `specs/bad-smell.md` section 5: Timer and Delay Analysis
- `specs/bad-smell.md` section 10: Artificial Delays in Tests

