when sending an email I receive this error `Message from server: {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":45,"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Error sending email: Error parsing API response: Unexpected end of JSON input"}]}}`

Reason is that responseData is empty.

I fixed parsing empty response by changing graph-api.js

ORIGINAL
```
            try {
              const jsonResponse = JSON.parse(responseData);
              resolve(jsonResponse);
            } catch (error) {
              reject(new Error(`Error parsing API response: ${error.message}`));
            }
```

FIX
```
            try {
		 responseData = responseData ? responseData : '{}';      <<< Added this line
              const jsonResponse = JSON.parse(responseData);
              resolve(jsonResponse);
            } catch (error) {
              reject(new Error(`Error parsing API response: ${error.message}`));
            }
