issue:
#### Issue #171: ClipVitB32 intermittently returns random results after update to v5.0

Hi

After updating to v5.0, the TextEmbedding no longer returns consistent results. It seems to return a random embedding vector sometimes.

To reproduce:

```rust
let q = "red car";
let mut fe = fastembed::TextEmbedding::try_new(fastembed::InitOptions::new(fastembed::EmbeddingModel::ClipVitB32)).unwrap();
let mut first = None;
for i in 0..100 {
    let vec = fe.embed(vec![q], None).unwrap();
    if first.is_none() {
        first = Some(vec[0].clone());
    } else {
        if vec[0] != *first.as_ref().unwrap() {
            println!("Embedding changed after {} iterations", i);
            println!("{:?}\n{:?}", first.as_ref().unwrap(), vec[0]);
            break;
        }
    }
}
```

This works fine with 4.9.1, but fails in 5.0

