#### Issue #890: Serialization of example value does not use SerializerSettings from JsonSchemaGeneratorSettings

I generate a JSON schema via reflection in a project using NSwag. All enums should be serialized as strings. So my `SerializerSettings` contain a `StringEnumConverter`.

I also want to provide meaningful example values for use in Swagger UI. I realize this by means of a custom `ISchemaProcessor` that sets the `SchemaProcessorContext.Schema.Example` property.

However, the resulting schema is inconsistent. While the actual type definition does define a string based enum, the example value uses an integer value. 

As a workaround I manually added a `[JsonConverter(typeof(StringEnumConverter))]` attribute to the affected property. Then the example value is serialized correctly.

I have attached a unit test project reproducing the issue: [JsonSchemaGenerationIssue.zip](https://github.com/RSuter/NJsonSchema/files/2811934/JsonSchemaGenerationIssue.zip)


